//   A:   i x k
//   B:   k x j
//   tmp: i x j
//   C:   j x l
//   D:   i x l
//
// Optimizations applied:
//   - Data layout:
//       * B: k is contiguous   -> good locality in the k-reduction of phase 1
//       * C: j is contiguous   -> good locality in the j-reduction of phase 2
//   - Cache blocking (tiling) using into_blocks_dynamic on i,j,k,l
//   - Traversal order chosen so that:
//       * phase 1 inner loop is over k (unit-stride in A and B)
//       * phase 2 inner loop is over j (unit-stride in tmp and C)
//   - Accumulation kept in registers for each (i,j) / (i,l) pair.
